==English==
[[Image:Barracuda.JPG|thumb|a typical '''barracuda'''<br> ({{taxlink|Sphyraena sphyraena|species}})]]

===Etymology===
First attested in the 1670s, from Latin American {{bor|en|es|barracuda}}, perhaps from a {{der|en|sai-car|-}} word.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌbæɹəˈkuːdə/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-barracuda.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːdə|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|barracuda|s}}

# Any large marine fish of the genus {{taxfmt|Sphyraena|genus}} that have elongated bodies, a projecting lower jaw, displaying prominent fang-shaped teeth, and are aggressive predators.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} One who uses harsh or predatory means to [[compete]].

